            {
                "entry_id": "ab43dd57-3a9e-3efd-a13c-e3b651068407",
                "word": "sharper",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "59b2a73e-50a8-441a-9518-b06ca8355aa0",
                        "entry_id": "ab43dd57-3a9e-3efd-a13c-e3b651068407",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sharpers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5d2edb23-5334-3894-8711-2e8d078d0673",
                        "entry_id": "ab43dd57-3a9e-3efd-a13c-e3b651068407",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A swindler; a cheat; a professional gambler who makes his living by cheating."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "71a255ba-4fa9-4cb3-a1f2-489ed0fa5558",
                                "sense_id": "5d2edb23-5334-3894-8711-2e8d078d0673",
                                "text": "I could plainly diſcover from whence one Family derives a long Chin; why a ſecond hath abounded with Knaves for two Generations, and Fools for two more; why a third happened to be crack-brained, and a fourth to be Sharpers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4175b89d-3c1a-4316-b418-446db077dfdb",
                                "sense_id": "5d2edb23-5334-3894-8711-2e8d078d0673",
                                "text": "Our young gentlemen who go to Rome will do well to be upon their guard against a set of sharpers, (some of them of our own country,) who deal in pictures and antiques, and very often impose upon the uninformed stranger, by selling him trash, as the productions of the most celebrated artists."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f61883b3-740a-4faa-8108-a501db1a3340",
                                "sense_id": "5d2edb23-5334-3894-8711-2e8d078d0673",
                                "text": "He was a man whom scarcely any amount of fortune could have benefited permanently, and who was made to be ruined, to cheat small tradesmen, to be the victim of astuter sharpers …"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "574e503c-1ab8-446d-9d9f-2ddc3455f95c",
                                "sense_id": "5d2edb23-5334-3894-8711-2e8d078d0673",
                                "text": "1878, John Payne, Introduction, in François Villon, Poems, translated by John Payne, New York: Boni & Liveright, c. 1918, p. 33 https://archive.org/details/poemsvillon00vill\n[…] in a twinkling the accomplished sharper changes the pitchers and pretending to examine the contents, asks the tapster what kind of wine he has given him […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6368a935-3979-42a1-af6c-bdefafeb2a32",
                                "sense_id": "5d2edb23-5334-3894-8711-2e8d078d0673",
                                "text": "1882, W. S. Gilbert, \"Emily, John, James, and I: A Derby Legend\" in The \"Bab\" Ballads, Philadelphia: David McKay, publishing date not given, p. 275, https://archive.org/details/babballads00gilb\nThe Derby Day sun glittered gaily on cads, / On maidens with gamboge hair, / On sharpers and pickpockets, swindlers and pads— / (For I, with my harp, was there)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "04d23d70-f1b1-4898-b2a4-53cc9ef11074",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab43dd57-3a9e-3efd-a13c-e3b651068407",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d2edb23-5334-3894-8711-2e8d078d0673",
                        "source_sense_description": "cheat, card-sharper",
                        "target_lang_word": "шу́лер",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "шу́лер",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "215d0d33-d485-310d-916c-3376361f2e9f",
                                        "entry_id": "471d89ff-b6bf-3090-9f78-5ea55ffd3212",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "карт. игрок, использующий нечестные, мошеннические приёмы в карточной игре"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff73358c-b322-4b1f-b673-360b83633173",
                                                "sense_id": "215d0d33-d485-310d-916c-3376361f2e9f",
                                                "text": "Мелкие станционные шулера приставали с просьбами поставить карточку или заложить банчик."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d27fea93-46af-478b-b37a-48fa77f03008",
                                                "sense_id": "215d0d33-d485-310d-916c-3376361f2e9f",
                                                "text": "Конечно, столь приметный крап был шулерами использован, и, по словам Ракова, он особенно годился для игры в польский банк, где понтирующий, как известно, получив три карты и идя втемную, выигрывает вдвое против названной суммы."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65eeb898-a407-4107-b8f3-5d710be99d58",
                                                "sense_id": "215d0d33-d485-310d-916c-3376361f2e9f",
                                                "text": "Левицкий, не слушая, встревал, рвался сообщить что-то про шулеров, которых он якобы всегда самолично бил канделябрами ― да, канделябрами их, по мордасам, по мордасам!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eff967c6-adcf-3405-8805-318c5f59ab20",
                                        "entry_id": "471d89ff-b6bf-3090-9f78-5ea55ffd3212",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "перен., разг. мошенник, обманщик"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b065412c-c960-4464-9adf-1d7a40023519",
                                                "sense_id": "eff967c6-adcf-3405-8805-318c5f59ab20",
                                                "text": "Биржевых шулеров, спекулянтов и лоточников здесь не сыщешь."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
